wip(heatmap): migrate the type filter onto the shared filterStore

Heatmap manager + persistence + tests migrated OFF filterOwner and onto the
shared per-map filterStore (Measure did this first in 9f1b2dba).

- manager.ts: layerFilters Map + filtersTouched field dropped; a per-source
  filterHost {normalize, apply, dimensions, counts} is registered per source
  via ensureFilterHost(sourceId); seedDeclaredFilter now declaration-only
  (setDeclaration, never persisted); renderHexagons reads the store; the
  departure and reset paths use store drop/reset. createPersisted keeps style
  fields + field, writes no filters/filtersTouched (old key read ONCE to
  migrate).
- persistence.ts: applySavedConfig migrates the old record's filters ONCE
  (filtersTouched===false -> setDeclaration per source; else restore per
  source, value+touched). SavedConfig type still carries filters/filtersTouched
  for the one-read migration.
- filterStore.ts: revalidate(layerId,name,transform) added (aligns a stored
  filter with the rebuilt snapshot without applying/publishing); restore is
  now a WRITE (value+touched, no normalize/apply) and resolve() is the read.
- tests: manager.test.ts rewritten to the store API (fsGet/fsHas/fsSize
  helpers + FILTER_STORE_KEY assertions); filterStore.test.ts +31 lines
  (revalidate + declaration-only persistence + same-name-different-layer).

NOT COMPLETE: 9 of 248 manager tests still fail (field-save restore was added
after this snapshot; malformed-filter migration + source-listing semantics +
declaration-ownership seeding need alignment). Remaining steps per lead:
LayerControl filter segment + filterOwner.ts deletion, then the store guard
grep.